        "original_id": "91320253-faad-5c7b-8d7a-bce098db957c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Timothy Nolen, Neil Patrick Harris, George Hearn, Patti LuPone\n- Works: Sweeney Todd, Great Performances, Doogie Howser, M.D., How I Met Your Mother, A Series of Unfortunate Events\n- Organizations: PBS, New York Philharmonic\n- Roles: Judge Turpin, Barney Stinson, Count Olaf\n\nFacts:\n- From 1989 to 1993, Neil Patrick Harris played the title character on the television series \"Doogie Howser, M.D.\"\n- In 2000, Timothy Nolen performed the role of Judge Turpin in a concert version of \"Sweeney Todd\" broadcast on PBS's \"Great Performances\" with the New York Philharmonic, George Hearn, Patti LuPone, and Neil Patrick Harris.\n- From 2005 to 2014, Neil Patrick Harris played Barney Stinson on \"How I Met Your Mother\" and received four Emmy Award nominations for the role.\n- From 2017 onward, Neil Patrick Harris played Count Olaf on \"A Series of Unfortunate Events.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
